  <h2 id="certificates">Official credential or institute certificate</h2>

  <p>
    This is where most money is lost. The right order is: free content, free practice system, then official certification only if a job requires it. Most fresher hiring asks for a degree, but the SAP-specific part is the part you can learn cheaply, and a certificate matters less than being able to run a process. Information is free; structure and feedback are what you pay for. As a planning heuristic, keep any single course or credential to roughly 10% of your whole learning budget, treat above about 20% as a serious caution that needs course-specific evidence, and avoid loans for a certificate.
  </p>

